window.AUDIT_NOTES = ["<b>Source: the IBU Deckhand Bid 196 Final-Final sheet, Nov 2, 2026 – Feb 28, 2027 (issued Oct 13, 2026; file “IBU Bid 196 11.2.26-2.28.27 Final-Final.pdf”).</b> 39 bids, the same count as Bid 195. Bids #1–33 are identical on the Masters Bid 196 Final-Final; the captain-only lines (#34–36 Extra Board, Bay Cruise A/B) come from the Masters and MMP Final sheets. Versus the Oct 12 deckhand book and the Masters draft the final sheet changed three things: #19 now prints a fixed report time (14:00), #27 Sat/Sun prints the new 14:50 and 17:05 Vallejo departures, and the Masters sheet now agrees with the 12:15 report on #16 Mon–Wed and #17 Thu/Fri. Report times, days off, crew sizes and every printed departure come straight from the sheet. Bid numbers changed — a Bid 196 number is not the same job as the Bid 195 number.", "<b>How the stop-by-stop times were built:</b> each printed departure was matched to the Nov 2, 2026 SF Bay Ferry timetable for its arrival time. When the boat ends a run away from its next departure, the earliest public trip that gets it there was added as an <i>implied</i> run (dashed). If no public trip connects in time, a light run (no passengers) is shown.", "<b><b>Official Nov 2 timetable (re-checked Oct 15, 2026 against sfbayferry.com):</b> every printed and implied sailing was walked through the live route pages (schedule effective Mar 9, 2026) with the Nov 2, 2026 schedule-change notice applied. 250 of 252 sailings match exactly. The two that don’t: #4’s FB/JLS 08:40 (the timetable trip is 08:35, but the boat is still arriving from Richmond — kept at 08:40 as printed) and #3’s 10:25 Oakland arrival (printed 11:00 on the timetable as a leftover of the dropped Alameda Main St call; shown 10:50). Corrected on this pass: the Seaplane 15:25 eastbound (#11) is the official Nov 2 time — the earlier check had it as 15:35 by mistake. Still printed with pre-Nov 2 times on the sheet: #27 Sat/Sun VJO 12:40 and 15:50 (official 12:45 / 15:55 — shown).", "<b>South San Francisco is suspended Nov 1–30, 2026</b> for dredging (resumes Dec 1). Bids #6, #7, #8, #9, #15, #16, #17 have South SF runs; the sheet assigns maintenance, cleaning, fueling or shift coverage instead during November. Those runs are greyed on the maps.", "<b>Light runs:</b> bids #6, #7, #8, #9, #16, #17 need the boat repositioned with no passengers somewhere in the shift (mostly around South SF and the Vallejo/Mare Island starts).", "<b>“AO 22:15” on Bid 19 weekends</b> is shown as the 22:15 Ferry Bldg → AMS → Oakland trip, the only weekend 22:15 sailing that serves Alameda Main St.", "<b>Maps:</b> GSHHG full-resolution coastline; the Oakland Estuary, Mare Island Strait and Seaplane Lagoon are drawn in by hand. Paths follow the real navigation lanes, not each captain's exact track.", "<b>Colours:</b> SF Bay Ferry's printed timetables — Oakland &amp; Alameda #4FAB47, Seaplane #E07B27, Harbor Bay #C7485D, Richmond #104676, South SF #862985, Vallejo #118B98; brand navy #015088."];

